<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chungnyeol of Goryeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1236">1236</a>–1308</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chungnyeol of Goryeo was king of Goryeo from 1274 to 1298 and again from 1298 to 1308. As crown prince he married a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>, making the Goryeo kings imperial sons-in-law of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>. During his reign Goryeo supplied ships and troops for the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasions-of-japan">Mongol invasions of Japan</a> in 1274 and 1281.</p></div>
